---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../i18n';
import { resolvePageSeo } from '../config/seo';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ContactSupportSection from '../components/ContactSupportSection.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const seo = resolvePageSeo('/support/');
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Support', path: '/support/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  logoAlt="Support – site logo"
  jsonLd={[
    webPageSchema({
      name: t.support.title,
      description: t.support.subtitle,
      url: '/support/',
    }),
    breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  ]}
>
  <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/20 py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSupportSection titleId="support-page-title" showTicketTips />

  <article class="border-t border-border bg-muted/10 py-10 md:py-14">
    <div class="prose prose-sm dark:prose-invert mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 text-muted-foreground">
      <h2 class="text-foreground">Before you contact support</h2>
      <p>
        Confirm which checkout you used: the main Black Ops 7 package, the optional Hyper-V Cloud DMA license, or the standalone HWID
        utility. Each listing has different Windows, virtualization, and billing requirements, so the product name on your receipt speeds
        up troubleshooting.
      </p>
      <p>
        Many setup questions are already answered in our
        <a href="/faq/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">pre-purchase FAQ index</a>. If your issue is compatibility
        related, work through the
        <a href="/guides/bo7-cheat-requirements/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Windows PC compatibility checklist</a>
        first and note any item that does not match your DxDiag export.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-foreground">Product-specific context</h2>
      <p>
        Cloud DMA buyers should capture Hyper-V role errors, GREENWARD activation status, and whether a static server or AWS line item is
        still pending. Read the
        <a href="/cloud-dma/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Cloud DMA Hyper-V licensing overview</a> so support knows
        which third-party components you already purchased.
      </p>
      <p>
        HWID utility orders should include whether Ricochet was running, your Windows build number, and whether Core Isolation or TPM
        settings changed since install. The
        <a href="/hwid-spoofer/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Black Ops 7 HWID utility page</a> lists the fields we
        compare against operator tickets.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-foreground">What to include in every ticket</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Order email and approximate purchase time (main, Cloud DMA, or HWID).</li>
        <li>Windows edition, build number, and whether Hyper-V or HVCI is enabled.</li>
        <li>Exact error text from the loader, portal, or virtualization dialog—screenshots help.</li>
        <li>Whether you recently changed BIOS virtualization, Secure Boot, or antivirus settings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you have not purchased yet, compare plan pricing on the
        <a href="/#products" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Black Ops 7 plan comparison</a> and mention which modules
        you intend to enable so we can confirm they match your PC.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-foreground">Main product troubleshooting</h2>
      <p>
        Portal login failures often trace to mismatched Windows builds or antivirus quarantining the loader. Attach the build number from
        Settings → System → About and mention whether Defender controlled folder access is enabled. If modules fail to toggle, list which
        features you expected from the homepage grid so we can confirm they are included in your plan tier.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stream-proof or overlay questions should include your capture software and whether you run the game in fullscreen exclusive or borderless
        mode. These details determine whether the issue is configuration-related or requires operator escalation.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-foreground">Response expectations</h2>
      <p>
        We reply during business hours in UTC+5 and prioritize tickets that include complete diagnostics. Duplicate messages slow the queue—
        update your original email thread instead of opening a second ticket. When an issue requires operator intervention, we explain what
        to forward to their billing desk so you are not bounced between two support teams.
      </p>
      <p>
        Refund or chargeback requests must go to the operator named on your receipt. We can clarify which product page you used before checkout,
        but we cannot modify transactions completed on external portals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
